{
  "_doc": "Skater pose keyframes (client only; read by src/client/skater/poses.ts). Stance space, regular stance (goofy, from data/rider.json, is drawn mirrored): vectors [n, f, u] = toward the nose, toward the toe side (where the rider faces), up; metres. Rotations [yaw, pitch, lean] in degrees: yaw turns the chest toward the nose, pitch bends forward, lean tips toward the nose. Feet: pos is on the grip when board = 1 (u = lift above the deck) and in the rider frame when board = 0 (u = height above the ground); toe = foot angle from across-the-board toward the nose; tilt + = toes up. Hands: pos is relative to the shoulders when board = 0. Board: lift (m), pitch (+ nose up) and yaw (+ nose toward the toe side) about pivot (-1 tail tip, -0.5 rear wheels, 0 centre, 0.5 front wheels, 1 nose tip), roll tweak (deg, + lifts the heel edge), n/f shift (m). Grind poses are written frontside (far side of the rail = toe side); backside mirrors yaw, roll and f. Poses list only what differs from base, or from the pose named in from. flipPivot: where a flip turns about, [n, u] off the deck centre (the impossible wraps round the back foot). flipTilt: degrees a flip stands the board up end on half way round (+ nose up; the hardflip passes near vertical between the legs, tail up). lipFrame: which way the rider stands on the coping for a lip trick: deck (default, the nose out over the deck), ramp (turned round, the nose over the ramp: disaster, tail stall), along (on the coping: axle stall); the board is seated on the coping and deck as for a slide on a ledge (an axle stall's hangers as for a grind). grindsTop / slidesTop: the pose on an obstacle with a top on the far side (a ledge, coping, a curb, a car roof; the view probes the park 12 cm out), where it differs from the rail one: the far wheels rest on the top (a 50-50 tips toward the approach side, a feeble's front truck lies on the top, a boardslide on a ledge pitches up over its far truck). Whatever the pose, the view seats the board on the line (poses.ts seat: the grinding truck's hanger on the edge, a slide's underside on it); tests/trickcontact.test.ts checks nothing goes through the ledge or rail. timing: flipTurnFrom/To/Ease ease the board's turn from the sim's trick progress so it is fastest off the flick and round when the feet catch (catch: feet on the bolts); grindLock (m) dips the knees over grindLockTicks as the trucks bite; grindArms and manualArms move the hands against the balance, windmill near the edge; lookAlong turns the head down the rail; revertTicks is the revert's swivel and revertSettle its crouch; slideTwist (deg) lags the shoulders behind a powerslide's swing. follow: weight and follow-through over the keyframes (poses.ts Follow): damped responses to the landing (by its impact), the pop, the grind lock-on and the push stroke; the hips move at once, the chest, head and arms a quarter period later, so they keep going and come back past rest.",
